\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 1. Business model\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 I manage digital marketing for a single advertiser: Juliana Capucci, a licensed clinical psychologist in Brazil (professional registration CRP 06/209216) who provides online psychotherapy sessions by video call.\
The business is a solo clinical practice. Revenue comes directly from therapy sessions paid by the patient. There is no reselling of advertising services, no agency operation, and no third-party clients. I am the only person who will use the tool, and the only advertiser account involved is the practice's own account.\
The practice's capacity is limited to roughly one to four new patients per month, so the advertising objective is not volume. It is to keep the cost per acquired patient within a known range and to stop spending when the schedule fills. That constraint is what drives the reporting need described below.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 2. What the tool does\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The tool is an internal, read-only reporting and analysis assistant. It runs on my own laptop and answers questions about the practice's own Google Ads account.\
It is built from two off-the-shelf components:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Google Ads MCP Server
\f1\b0  \'97 the official open-source server published by Google at 
\f2\i github.com/googleads/google-ads-mcp
\f1\i0 , installed locally via pipx and run as a local stdio process. It is read-only by design and exposes three tools: 
\f2\i search
\f1\i0 , 
\f2\i get_resource_metadata
\f1\i0  and 
\f2\i list_accessible_customers
\f1\i0 .\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Claude Code
\f1\b0  \'97 a command-line AI assistant that connects to the local MCP server and turns my questions into GAQL queries, then summarises the results.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 I did not build a hosted product. There is no web application, no user accounts, no database of Google Ads data, and nothing exposed to the internet.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 3. Why the API rather than the user interface\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Three recurring reporting tasks are slow and error-prone in the interface and are the reason for this application:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Weekly search-terms review.
\f1\b0  Reading the search terms report and building the negative keyword list is the single most cost-saving routine early in a campaign. Querying it directly makes the review consistent instead of ad hoc.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Cost per acquired patient.
\f1\b0  Google Ads reports cost per conversion, but a conversion here is a WhatsApp click. The figure that matters is cost per patient who actually started therapy, which requires joining campaign cost data with an offline record I keep separately.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Campaign and keyword performance summaries
\f1\b0  across a small number of ad groups segmented by patient profile.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

